Often, the mountainous surroundings provided the backdrop for Sholay scenes, although the film did not require much space to shoot. The production crew had to build a road to connect the Bangalore highway with Ramanagara to make the sets more accessible. Art director Ram Yedekar created an entire town on the location. A prison set was also built outdoors near Rajkamal Studio in Mumbai to match the natural lighting during on-location shoots. For a period of time, one section of Ramanagara was referred to as " Sippy Nagar " in honor of the film's director. Today, tourists passing through Ramanagara still receive a visit to the " Sholay rocks ", where most of the film was shot.
